0..71 Comment "// What a recursion handed through a higher-order function refuses. The"
72..148 Comment "// recursion\'s own parameter handed to `apply` or `applyAt` instantiates its"
149..227 Comment "// parameter or stage at that parameter\'s stage, which the claim does not take"
228..294 Comment "// . A helper whose signature names no type parameter and no stage"
295..370 Comment "// hands its argument on at no stage, and a helper with no recursion and no"
371..439 Comment "// stage opens none for its result to follow: the model\'s quantified"
440..516 Comment "// signatures lift both, `applyAt` the first and `predAt` the second. A call"
517..592 Comment "// whose arguments bound one stage binder where no stage fits is refused by"
593..671 Comment "// name, and so is a stage supplied by name, `applyAt[.i = k]`, apart from the"
672..738 Comment "// one the arguments show or for a binder they do not show. Shared"
739..791 Comment "// with `../../model/data/sized-higher-order.gandr`."
792..794 Comment "//"
795..829 Comment "// - see: #393 — `applied_again`"
830..893 Comment "// - see: #392 — `applied_at_again`, `integerAt`, `carriedAt`"
894..963 Comment "// - see: #1227 — `disagreeing`, `suppliedApart`, `suppliedUnshown`"
964..1007 Comment "// - see: #1241 — `looping_through_bound`"
1009..1051 Comment "// The naturals the recursions take apart."
